                <pb facs="0627" n="507" sameAs="frus:frus1922v01/pg507"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">723.2515/1000: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Chargé in Peru</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Sterling</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-08-01T15:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">August 1,
                                1922—3 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>53. Chilean Chargé d’Affaires has called Department’s attention to the fact that
                    the Arbitral Protocol, recently signed in Washington between Chile and Peru,
                    provides for ratification thereof, the ratifications to be exchanged in
                    Washington, but that no such provision is made with respect to Complementary
                    Act. He stated that his Government does not attach great importance to the
                    matter but desires to know the views of the Peruvian Government as to whether
                    ratification of the Complementary Act is necessary or not. Ascertain attitude of
                    Peruvian Government and cable reply.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hughes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
